{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-8d53dda6-ec24-496e-8ca4-22ac55a58b27","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-892aaa63093b7c97","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-tpsk22jc/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E007.md","content":"# Observability instrumentation in maas-api (metrics and structured logging)\n\n## Description\n\nInstruments maas-api with the observability the strategy makes a core value proposition for MaaS\non xKS: Prometheus metrics (P0) and structured JSON logging (P1) covering token usage, rate\nlimiting enforcement, API key lifecycle, and authentication/validation decisions. The\nimplementation vehicle (in the MaaS 3.4 GA baseline vs. a post-3.4 patch) is determined by the\nbaseline changeability assessment; if the baseline is frozen, the instrumentation ships as a\npost-3.4 patch or is deferred per the strategy.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Prometheus `/metrics` endpoint in maas-api exposing: token usage per user/subscription, rate\n  limiting enforcement events, API key lifecycle events (creation, validation, revocation), and\n  inference request latency.\n- Metrics per the strategy's acceptance criteria: `maas_api_key_created_total`,\n  `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`,\n  `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`.\n- Structured JSON logs for authentication decisions, API key validation, and subscription\n  selection, formatted for aggregation in CKS Grafana Loki.\n- Asynchronous metric emission to bound latency overhead (mitigation if p99 overhead exceeds\n  5 ms: move emission to post-response goroutines).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a deployed MaaS instance with Prometheus integration, when a user creates an API key,\n  makes inference requests, and exceeds a rate limit, then Prometheus metrics include\n  `maas_api_key_created_total`, `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`, and\n  `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`, measured by querying the\n  Prometheus instance.\n- Given structured logging enabled, when an authentication event occurs (success or failure), the\n  log entry includes timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision\n  (allow/deny), and reason (if denied).\n- Log output is structured JSON suitable for Loki aggregation with label filters.\n- Instrumentation overhead stays within the strategy's performance mitigation bound (p99 < 5 ms,\n  async emission otherwise).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Observability metrics functional: token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key\n  lifecycle events.\n- [P1] Observability logging functional (maas-api portion: authentication events, API key\n  validation, subscription selection).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":67605,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90b1b6f56466ed62","agent_id":"a8a2b528182aa5e23","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"ced060a2-1013-4b77-a949-494d2af857b1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:00:35.202Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
