\t  all proceed regardless of RHCL's commitment, because the standalone Authorino + Limitador\n196\t  fallback keeps the deployment viable.\n197\t- **Tier 2 (mechanism-gated work)**: E008, E009, E010, E011, E012 — full-stack deployment\n198\t  validation and everything downstream of it wait on E001's mechanism decision. Tier 2 is\n199\t  soft-gated: if RHCL does not commit, the fallback ladder (standalone Helm, then direct Envoy\n200\t  ext_authz) keeps Tier 2 moving, with the escalation to product leadership recorded per the\n201\t  strategy.\n202\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a28edd69652dfb8f","agent_id":"aa81afe1864591cbd","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"4ff3f3bb-ad4d-487d-b71a-4d680c3bcf95","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:05:13.417Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ade2f92f7a491373","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
