{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93ed3ffdaacdb411","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E003\n3\ttitle: Validate CKS observability infrastructure accessibility\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Monitoring\n6\tteam: xKS Platform\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate CKS observability infrastructure accessibility\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tValidates the strategy's assumption that CKS (CoreWeave Kubernetes Service) provides standard\n30\tobservability infrastructure — a Prometheus instance able to scrape MaaS metrics endpoints and\n31\tGrafana Loki log aggregation accessible for MaaS workload logs. This is infrastructure not in the\n32\tplatform inventory, so its existence and accessibility must be confirmed before the observability\n33\tintegration work commits to an approach; if inaccessible, dedicated observability provisioning\n34\tbecomes part of the scope.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Confirm the CKS Prometheus instance can scrape MaaS `/metrics` endpoints (scrape target\n39\t  reachability, required annotations or scrape configuration).\n40\t- Confirm Loki ingests and makes queryable the logs of the namespaces where MaaS will deploy\n41\t  (label filters usable for MaaS logs).\n42\t- Document any access requirements, provisioning gaps, or configuration needed from CoreWeave /\n43\t  the xKS Platform side.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Prometheus scrape of a representative MaaS-style `/metrics` endpoint on CKS is confirmed\n48\t  working (or the gap and remediation documented).\n49\t- Loki aggregation of workload logs from the MaaS target namespace is confirmed queryable with\n50\t  label filters (or the gap and remediation documented).\n51\t- Findings are documented, including any access coordination required with CoreWeave.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- Enables [P0] Observability metrics functional (infrastructure validation portion).\n56\t- Enables [P1] Observability logging functional (infrastructure validation portion).\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a28edd69652dfb8f","agent_id":"aa81afe1864591cbd","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"dca664eb-8daf-43e2-a374-7ca30ae0e294","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:05:19.920Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-93ed3ffdaacdb411","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
