{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5d3efa40123f503","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E004\n3\ttitle: Helm chart packaging for MaaS components on xKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Helm chart packaging for MaaS components on xKS\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tPackages the MaaS components (maas-api, maas-controller, payload-processing BBR ext_proc server)\n34\tas Helm charts for non-OpenShift Kubernetes, replacing the OLM-based operator installation used\n35\ton RHOAI. The charts make every OpenShift-specific dependency configurable so the same charts\n36\tdeploy on CKS (Istio), AKS, and other xKS platforms.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Helm charts for maas-api, maas-controller, and payload-processing with configurable values for:\n41\t  - Gateway class name (Istio for CKS; `envoy-gateway` multi-platform and\n42\t    `azure-application-gateway` for AKS as validated future options) instead of\n43\t    `openshift-default`.\n44\t  - OIDC issuer configuration (issuer URL, client ID, audience, group claim path).\n45\t  - TLS certificate source via cert-manager instead of OpenShift service-CA auto-generated\n46\t    certificates.\n47\t  - PostgreSQL connection (shared with other RHAII components or dedicated — resolved at\n48\t    deployment time, both supported).\n49\t- Removal of OpenShift-specific assumptions from the deployment manifests.\n50\t- Integration of the charts with the RHAII xKS deployment/installation strategy, in collaboration\n51\t  with the xKS Platform team.\n52\t- Build and publication of the charts through the RHAII build pipeline (Helm chart build pipeline\n53\t  onboarding is a pending process gate per the strategy's prerequisites).\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The chart installs maas-api, maas-controller, and payload-processing on a non-OpenShift\n58\t  Kubernetes cluster with all listed values configurable.\n59\t- TLS certificates are issued via cert-manager and rotation does not interrupt active requests.\n60\t- The MaaS HTTPRoute attaches to a configurable GatewayClass (Istio validated on CKS).\n61\t- The PostgreSQL connection (shared or dedicated) is chart-configurable.\n62\t- The chart is consumable by the RHAII xKS installation tooling (validated with the xKS Platform\n63\t  team).\n64\t- The chart is built and published via the RHAII build pipeline (build onboarding confirmed).\n65\t- License validation for any new chart dependencies is confirmed (pending process gate per the\n66\t  strategy's prerequisites).\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- Enables [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on CKS.\n71\t- Enables [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on AKS.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a28edd69652dfb8f","agent_id":"aa81afe1864591cbd","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"5d10c281-17fd-49b4-a5fc-07d1c5990217","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:05:23.951Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5d3efa40123f503","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
