{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfaf5d4d78a1a694","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E005\n3\ttitle: External OIDC authentication enablement in MaaS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the MaaS 3.4 GA baseline requires code changes to leverage\n15\t    external OIDC (not just configuration), rewrite the epic around the required code\n16\t    changes to the AuthPolicy generation and internal auth middleware; if the baseline\n17\t    cannot be changed at all, ship the OIDC enablement as a post-3.4 patch.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# External OIDC authentication enablement in MaaS\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tReplaces OpenShift-specific identity infrastructure (KubernetesTokenReview against the OpenShift\n40\tAPI server) with external OIDC validation for MaaS on xKS. Customers provide their own\n41\tOIDC-compatible identity provider (Keycloak, Entra ID, Google Identity Platform, Cognito, or\n42\tother standards-compliant providers). The API key authentication flow (`sk-oai-*` bearer tokens\n43\tvalidated via the maas-api callback endpoint) is OIDC-agnostic and remains unchanged — its\n44\tcontinued function on xKS is validated here.\n45\t\n46\tThe approach is gated on the MaaS 3.4 GA baseline changeability assessment: the strategy expects\n47\tbasic OIDC integration to be a configuration change (the Tenant CRD already supports\n48\t`oidcIssuerURL`, `oidcClientID`, `oidcAudience`), but if the baseline requires code changes the\n49\tapproach is rewritten accordingly.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- Configure the MaaS-generated AuthPolicy resources to use Authorino's `oidc` identity source\n54\t  (customer OIDC issuer URL and JWKS endpoint) instead of KubernetesTokenReview.\n55\t- Plumb OIDC issuer configuration through the Helm chart values and Tenant CRD fields.\n56\t- Adapt internal maas-api authentication paths that rely on Kubernetes TokenReview /\n57\t  SubjectAccessReview (OpenShift identity mapping) for the xKS deployment model.\n58\t- Preserve the API key validation callback path (`/internal/v1/api-keys/validate` via Authorino\n59\t  HTTP callback) and confirm it is unaffected by the OIDC change.\n60\t- Validate against at least one standards-compliant OIDC provider, with the design supporting\n61\t  varied providers (Entra ID, Cognito, Google Identity Platform).\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on xKS with OIDC configured, a user authenticating with a valid\n66\t  OIDC JWT token is authenticated; invalid or expired tokens are rejected.\n67\t- API key authentication (the `sk-oai-*` flow) functions on xKS without OIDC dependency:\n68\t  inference requests using valid API keys succeed.\n69\t- Failure mode: when the OIDC provider becomes unavailable, inference requests using valid API\n70\t  keys continue to succeed, while OIDC-authenticated requests fail with HTTP 503 and a\n71\t  descriptive error message.\n72\t- Backwards compatibility: no changes to RHOAI MaaS GA behavior — xKS changes are additive or\n73\t  configuration-driven.\n74\t- The OIDC identity flow works with at least one standards-compliant provider and the\n75\t  configuration surface supports provider-specific issuer/JWKS values.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- [P0] External OIDC authentication validated for user identity.\n80\t- [P0] API key authentication (`sk-oai-*` flow) functional on xKS.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a28edd69652dfb8f","agent_id":"aa81afe1864591cbd","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"f829809a-68db-469f-97b6-f26db2d6dba3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:05:24.734Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfaf5d4d78a1a694","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
