{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf5b96355e94f6b7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n3\ttitle: Deploy and validate MaaS on CKS and AKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E004\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E005\n14\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: rewrite\n17\t  fallback_approach: 'If RHCL official xKS support is not committed, deploy Kuadrant\n18\t    via the fallback ladder: standalone Authorino + Limitador via Helm, or direct\n19\t    Envoy ext_authz integration as contingency; the escalation to product leadership\n20\t    is recorded and the deployment approach rewritten accordingly.'\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: 0\n27\t  external_dependency: -1\n28\t  human_process_gates: 0\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\timplementation_type: null\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: High\n34\tai_implementability_score: 4\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\tbranch: null\n37\t---\n38\t# Deploy and validate MaaS on CKS and AKS\n39\t\n40\t## Description\n41\t\n42\tDeploys MaaS via the Helm charts on CKS first (the priority platform, with Istio GatewayClass and\n43\tmTLS configuration for CoreWeave's service mesh), then on AKS, and validates core MaaS\n44\tfunctionality: subscription/tier management, token rate limiting, API key authentication, and\n45\texternal OIDC authentication. Documents what works, what breaks, and the engineering delta —\n46\tfeeding the known-limitations documentation. The Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) underlay is\n47\tdeployed using the mechanism confirmed by the RHCL xKS support validation, with the strategy's\n48\tfallback ladder (standalone Authorino + Limitador via Helm; direct Envoy ext_authz contingency)\n49\tavailable if official RHCL support is not committed.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- Deploy MaaS on CKS via Helm with OIDC configuration and the Istio GatewayClass (including TLS\n54\t  and mTLS configuration for Istio control-plane integration).\n55\t- Deploy MaaS on AKS via Helm (GatewayClass per platform: `azure-application-gateway` or\n56\t  `envoy-gateway`).\n57\t- Validate core functionality on both platforms: subscription management, token rate limiting,\n58\t  API key lifecycle, OIDC authentication, tier mapping with OIDC group claims.\n59\t- Validate failure modes: OIDC provider unavailability, Limitador pod termination, cert-manager\n60\t  certificate rotation, PostgreSQL unavailability.\n61\t- Document what works vs. what breaks and the engineering delta (code changes, configuration\n62\t  changes, Helm chart packaging gaps).\n63\t\n64\t## Acceptance Criteria\n65\t\n66\t- Given a CKS cluster with RHCL/Kuadrant and Gateway API (Istio) installed, when MaaS is deployed\n67\t  via Helm chart with OIDC configuration, then the maas-api and maas-controller pods are running\n68\t  and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n69\t- Given an AKS cluster with RHCL/Kuadrant and Gateway API installed, when MaaS is deployed via\n70\t  Helm chart with OIDC configuration, then the maas-api and maas-controller pods are running and\n71\t  healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n72\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with OIDC configured, when a user authenticates with a\n73\t  valid OIDC JWT token and creates an API key, then the API key is persisted in PostgreSQL and\n74\t  can be used for model inference, measured by a successful inference request using the generated\n75\t  API key.\n76\t- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit,\n77\t  then Limitador returns HTTP 429, measured by monitoring response status codes.\n78\t- Failure mode — OIDC provider unavailable: API key requests continue to succeed; OIDC requests\n79\t  fail with HTTP 503 and a descriptive error.\n80\t- Failure mode — Limitador pod terminated: inference requests denied with HTTP 503, measured by\n81\t  response status and Envoy logs showing upstream connection failure.\n82\t- Failure mode — cert-manager TLS rotation: active inference requests continue without\n83\t  interruption; new requests succeed with the new certificate.\n84\t- Failure mode — PostgreSQL unavailable: API key creation fails with HTTP 503 and existing API\n85\t  key validation fails on cache miss, while OIDC token-based authentication continues to succeed.\n86\t- What works, what breaks, and the engineering delta are documented for both platforms.\n87\t\n88\t## HLR Traceability\n89\t\n90\t- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on CKS.\n91\t- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on AKS.\n92\t- [P0] Token rate limiting functional on xKS.\n93\t- [P0] External OIDC authentication validated for user identity.\n94\t- [P0] API key authentication (`sk-oai-*` flow) functional on xKS.\n95\t- [P1] Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims (validation portion).\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a28edd69652dfb8f","agent_id":"aa81afe1864591cbd","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"b356f86f-31a4-40b8-9de3-887e4ed8dccd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:05:28.864Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf5b96355e94f6b7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
