elm chart value for per-deployment configuration.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Given an OIDC deployment with a non-standard group claim format and `groupClaimPath` configured\n54\t  to match, a user with group membership authenticating is mapped to the appropriate subscription\n55\t  tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement.\n56\t- The default claim path preserves current RHOAI behavior (backwards compatible, additive change).\n57\t- Tier/subscription CRUD against OIDC group claims is functional.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- [P0] Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (supports Entra ID `groups`, Cognito\n62\t  `cognito:groups`, custom claims).\n63\t- [P1] Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a28edd69652dfb8f","agent_id":"aa81afe1864591cbd","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"2bc713f7-6a71-4852-b1d1-a6bfdacf3000","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:05:37.799Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ec5b3e51b18c377","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
