ing IdP outages (open question) | The failure-mode ACs already define required behavior; caching is an implementation decision | ACs on E005/E008 |\n121\t| What authentication approach for xKS (open question) | Resolved by the strategy itself: external OIDC with customer-provided IdP | Reflected in E005 scope |\n122\t\n123\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n124\t\n125\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n126\t| --- | --- | --- |\n127\t| MaaS successfully deployed on CKS | P0 | E008 |\n128\t| MaaS successfully deployed on AKS | P0 | E008 |\n129\t| Token rate limiting functional on xKS | P0 | E001 (mechanism), E008 (validation) |\n130\t| External OIDC authentication validated | P0 | E005, E008 |\n131\t| API key authentication (sk-oai-* flow) functional on xKS | P0 | E005 (flow preserved), E008 (validation) |\n132\t| Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping | P0 | BRANCH-A-E006 / BRANCH-B-E006 |\n133\t| RHCL official xKS support status confirmed, mechanism validated | P0 | E001 |\n134\t| Observability metrics functional | P0 | E007 (instrumentation), E009 (dashboards/Prometheus) |\n135\t| Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims | P1 | BRANCH-A-E006 / BRANCH-B-E006, E008 (validation) |\n136\t| Observability logging functional | P1 | E007 (maas-api logs), E010 (Authorino/Limitador logs), E009 (Loki aggregation) |\n137\t| Known limitations documented | P1 | E012 |\n138\t| User identity flow documented for xKS | P2 | E012 |\n139\t| Distributed tracing functional | P2 | E011 |\n140\t\n141\tAll 13 HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. Priority inheritance: E001/E002/E003 are P0\n142\tbecause they block P0 work. The P1 logging HLR is bundled into E007 (P0) because maas-api metrics\n143\tand structured logging share the same instrumentation surface — not distinct and deferrable per\n144\tStep 4. The P2 tracing HLR is split into E011: it is a distinct, deferrable feature with\n145\tindependent user value. E010 is P1 (its HLR is P1; it blocks no P0 work). E012