dless of RHCL's commitment, because the standalone Authorino + Limitador\n195\t  fallback keeps the deployment viable.\n196\t- **Tier 2 (mechanism-gated work)**: E008, E009, E010, E011, E012 — full-stack deployment\n197\t  validation and everything downstream of it wait on E001's mechanism decision. Tier 2 is\n198\t  soft-gated: if RHCL does not commit, the fallback ladder (standalone Helm, then direct Envoy\n199\t  ext_authz) keeps Tier 2 moving, with the escalation to product leadership recorded per the\n200\t  strategy.\n201\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a57964090eceb0b5","agent_id":"a4a6b6390e6cbdd43","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"ff14a951-e111-40f6-a8dd-b4a03f56f02c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:11:55.190Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba449c24873dffe7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
