  identity, method, reason).\n50\t- Structured logging configuration for Limitador rate limit enforcement (429 responses with\n51\t  exceeded quota).\n52\t- Log format compatible with CKS Grafana Loki aggregation and label-based querying.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with structured logging enabled, when an authentication\n57\t  event occurs (success or failure), then the Authorino log entry includes timestamp, user\n58\t  identity, authentication method, decision (allow/deny), and reason (if denied), measured by\n59\t  querying CKS Grafana Loki with label filters.\n60\t- Rate limit enforcement events (HTTP 429 with exceeded quota) are logged by Limitador in\n61\t  structured form and aggregated in Loki.\n62\t- TokenRateLimitPolicy behavior is confirmed unchanged on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (Limitador\n63\t  requires no code changes).\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- [P1] Observability logging functional (Authorino/Limitador portion: authentication events,\n68\t  rate limit enforcement).\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a57964090eceb0b5","agent_id":"a4a6b6390e6cbdd43","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"823ec9b2-7334-49df-9bbc-0ff7161c404d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:12:07.254Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8821b45fee4e6781","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
