g functional on xKS | P0 | E001 (mechanism), E008 (validation) |\n140\t| External OIDC authentication validated | P0 | E005, E008 |\n141\t| API key authentication (sk-oai-* flow) functional on xKS | P0 | E005 (flow preserved), E008 (validation) |\n142\t| Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping | P0 | BRANCH-A-E006 / BRANCH-B-E006 |\n143\t| RHCL official xKS support status confirmed, mechanism validated | P0 | E001 |\n144\t| Observability metrics functional | P0 | E007 (instrumentation), E009 (dashboards/Prometheus) |\n145\t| Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims | P1 | BRANCH-A-E006 / BRANCH-B-E006, E008 (validation) |\n146\t| Observability logging functional | P1 | E007 (maas-api logs), E010 (Authorino/Limitador logs), E009 (Loki aggregation) |\n147\t| Known limitations documented | P1 | E012 (consumes E013's engineering-delta findings) |\n148\t| User identity flow documented for xKS | P2 | E012 |\n149\t| Distributed tracing functional | P2 | E011 |\n150\t\n151\tAll 13 HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. Priority inheritance: E001/E002/E003 are P0\n152\tbecause they block P0 work. The P1 logging HLR is bundled into E007 (P0) because maas-api metrics\n153\tand structured logging share the same instrumentation surface — not distinct and deferrable per\n154\tStep 4. The P2 tracing HLR is split into E011: it is a distinct, deferrable feature with\n155\tindependent user value. E010 is P1 (its HLR is P1; it blocks no P0 work). E012 is P0 via the\n156\tdocs-authoring priority exception (strategy priority `Blocker` → Critical-equivalent → P0), not\n157\tvia inheritance.\n158\t\n159\t## Component Mappings (canonical names from .context/rhai-components.txt)\n160\t\n161\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Notes |\n162\t| --- | --- | --- |\n163\t| models-as-a-service (maas-api, maas-controller, payload-processing) | Model as a Service | Direct match; architecture context `models-as-a-service.md` exists |\n164\t| Kuadrant (Authorino