already exists in the platform, so no\n185\t   onboarding chain was generated (Rule 20 does not fire); the Helm build-pipeline need is an AC\n186\t   on E004 and license validation is noted there as an open process gate.\n187\t5. **Timeline risk.** MaaS 3.4 GA stable-build availability is flagged as a critical blocker for\n188\t   the Summit (May 2026) announcement; RC target April 27 has passed relative to the strategy's\n189\t   own dates. Captured in E002's scope and as a risk on E008; the RHOAI 3.3 fallback demo is the\n190\t   strategy's stated mitigation.\n191\t6. **CRD count discrepancy.** The strategy says maas-controller manages 5 CRDs; architecture\n192\t   context lists 8 reconciled custom resources. Informational only — no decomposition impact.\n193\t7. **PostgreSQL LRU cache.** The risk table proposes an in-memory LRU cache for validated API\n194\t   key hashes, but the failure-mode acceptance criteria accept degraded validation during\n195\t   PostgreSQL unavailability. Treated as an optional mitigation within E008, not a requirement.\n196\t\n197\t## Tiered Delivery\n198\t\n199\tThe RHCL official xKS support dependency has uncertain timing (external, status Unknown), and\n200\tpartial value is deliverable without it:\n201\t\n202\t- **Tier 1 (independent work)**: E002, E003, E004, E005, E007, and the selected E006 branch —\n203\t  baseline changeability, Helm packaging, OIDC authentication, and observability instrumentation\n204\t  all proceed regardless of RHCL's commitment, because the standalone Authorino + Limitador\n205\t  fallback keeps the deployment viable.\n206\t- **Tier 2 (mechanism-gated work)**: E008, E009, E010, E011, E012, E013 — full-stack deployment\n207\t  validation and everything downstream of it wait on E001's mechanism decision. Tier 2 is\n208\t  soft-gated: if RHCL does not commit, the fallback ladder (standalone Helm, then direct Envoy\n209\t  ext_authz) keeps Tier 2 moving, with the escalation to product leadership recorded per the\n210\t  strategy.\n211\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba431fd5c6e583b5","agent_id":"a56ac38aeba4300c7","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"6f26ca2a-2416-4ea4-bbb8-ab0ac956f670","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:19:50.132Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8902265713105cd3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
