{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0b39229cf73fbdc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n3\ttitle: Confirm RHCL xKS support and validate Kuadrant on CKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: RHCL / OpenShift\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Confirm RHCL xKS support and validate Kuadrant on CKS\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's strategic dependency on RHCL (Red Hat Common Libraries) for MaaS on xKS.\n30\tConfirms whether the OpenShift RHCL team commits to official xKS support and Helm-based\n31\tdistribution for Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador), and hands-on validates that Kuadrant installs\n32\tand functions on CKS with the Istio GatewayClass. The deliverable is a documented decision on the\n33\tMaaS xKS deployment mechanism for authentication and rate limiting, selected from the strategy's\n34\tpriority ladder: (1) official RHCL Helm charts, (2) standalone Authorino + Limitador via Helm,\n35\t(3) direct Envoy ext_authz integration. If RHCL support is not committed, the escalation to\n36\tproduct leadership is recorded and the fallback path is activated.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Engage the OpenShift RHCL team to obtain a commitment (or explicit non-commitment) and timeline\n41\t  for official xKS support and official Kuadrant Helm charts.\n42\t- Validate a Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) installation on a CKS cluster with the Istio\n43\t  GatewayClass, per the strategy's Sprint 1 validation task.\n44\t- Exercise the Authorino OIDC identity source and Limitador token rate limiting in that\n45\t  installation to confirm they function on non-OpenShift Kubernetes.\n46\t- Evaluate the fallback ladder (standalone Helm deployment; direct Envoy ext_authz contingency)\n47\t  and document which rung applies.\n48\t- If RHCL support is not committed: record the escalation to product leadership per the strategy.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- RHCL official xKS support status is documented (committed or not committed, with timeline).\n53\t- Kuadrant installability on CKS with Istio is validated with pass/fail evidence (pods running,\n54\t  AuthPolicy enforceable, TokenRateLimitPolicy enforceable).\n55\t- The deployment mechanism for MaaS xKS is selected from the priority ladder with rationale.\n56\t- If not committed: escalation to product leadership is recorded and the selected fallback\n57\t  (standalone Authorino + Limitador, or direct Envoy ext_authz) is documented with its\n58\t  implications for long-term support.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- [P0] RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated.\n63\t- [P0] Token rate limiting functional on xKS (mechanism validation portion).\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba431fd5c6e583b5","agent_id":"a56ac38aeba4300c7","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"a8854428-e4e7-4b8d-a37a-d33e637ed978","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:19:55.125Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0b39229cf73fbdc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
