{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b063a214bcfd085","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n3\ttitle: Assess MaaS 3.4 GA baseline changeability for xKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Assess MaaS 3.4 GA baseline changeability for xKS\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDetermines which xKS-enabling changes can be made in the MaaS 3.4 GA codebase before downstream\n30\timplementation work commits to an approach. Three questions from the strategy's open questions and\n31\tassumptions are resolved by one experiment (inspecting the 3.4 GA baseline and its release freeze\n32\tconstraints):\n33\t\n34\t1. Can the existing MaaS AuthPolicy generation leverage Authorino's external OIDC identity source\n35\t   without code changes, or are changes needed?\n36\t2. Can the Tenant CRD be extended with a `groupClaimPath` field, or is it frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA?\n37\t3. Can maas-api be instrumented with Prometheus metrics and structured logging within the\n38\t   baseline, or must the instrumentation ship as a post-3.4 patch (or be deferred)?\n39\t\n40\tAlso confirms MaaS 3.4 RC/stable build availability with the MaaS PM (code freeze passed late\n41\tMarch 2026; stable build delivery timing unknown — critical blocker for the Summit timeline).\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Inspect the MaaS 3.4 GA baseline: Tenant CRD spec (existing `oidcIssuerURL`, `oidcClientID`,\n46\t  `oidcAudience` fields; extensibility for a `groupClaimPath` field),\n47\t  MaaSAuthPolicyReconciler's AuthPolicy generation, and maas-api instrumentation surface.\n48\t- Determine release freeze constraints: whether CRD schema changes, controller changes, and\n49\t  maas-api changes may land in the baseline or require a post-3.4 patch vehicle.\n50\t- Confirm RC/stable build availability dates with the MaaS PM.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Each of the three questions has a documented answer with evidence from the baseline (file/CRD\n55\t  references), not conjecture.\n56\t- Explicit go/no-go on extending the Tenant CRD with `groupClaimPath`, selecting the conditional\n57\t  implementation branch for group claim mapping (code change vs. documented claim format).\n58\t- Recommended release vehicle (baseline change vs. post-3.4 patch vs. defer) for maas-api\n59\t  observability instrumentation.\n60\t- MaaS 3.4 build availability (RC and stable) confirmed with dates, or the timing risk escalated.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- Enables [P0] External OIDC authentication validated for user identity.\n65\t- Enables [P0] Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping.\n66\t- Enables [P0] Observability metrics functional.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba431fd5c6e583b5","agent_id":"a56ac38aeba4300c7","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"9fd8bcf1-1ff1-4b19-94be-cc73fbf1aed3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:19:55.911Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b063a214bcfd085","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
