{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9631f1b721b64b7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E007\n3\ttitle: Observability instrumentation in maas-api (metrics and structured logging)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If maas-api is frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA, ship the instrumentation\n15\t    as a post-3.4 patch; if patching is not feasible in the Dev Preview window, defer\n16\t    the metrics/logging work to P1 per the strategy.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 3\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Observability instrumentation in maas-api (metrics and structured logging)\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tInstruments maas-api with the observability the strategy makes a core value proposition for MaaS\n39\ton xKS: Prometheus metrics (P0) and structured JSON logging (P1) covering token usage, rate\n40\tlimiting enforcement, API key lifecycle, and authentication/validation decisions. The\n41\timplementation vehicle (in the MaaS 3.4 GA baseline vs. a post-3.4 patch) is determined by the\n42\tbaseline changeability assessment; if the baseline is frozen, the instrumentation ships as a\n43\tpost-3.4 patch or is deferred per the strategy.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Prometheus `/metrics` endpoint in maas-api exposing: token usage per user/subscription, rate\n48\t  limiting enforcement events, API key lifecycle events (creation, validation, revocation), and\n49\t  inference request latency.\n50\t- Metrics per the strategy's acceptance criteria: `maas_api_key_created_total`,\n51\t  `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`,\n52\t  `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`.\n53\t- Structured JSON logs for authentication decisions, API key validation, and subscription\n54\t  selection, formatted for aggregation in CKS Grafana Loki.\n55\t- Asynchronous metric emission to bound latency overhead (mitigation if p99 overhead exceeds\n56\t  5 ms: move emission to post-response goroutines).\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance with Prometheus integration, when a user creates an API key,\n61\t  makes inference requests, and exceeds a rate limit, then Prometheus metrics include\n62\t  `maas_api_key_created_total`, `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`, and\n63\t  `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`, measured by querying the\n64\t  Prometheus instance.\n65\t- Given structured logging enabled, when an authentication event occurs (success or failure), the\n66\t  log entry includes timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision\n67\t  (allow/deny), and reason (if denied).\n68\t- Log output is structured JSON suitable for Loki aggregation with label filters.\n69\t- Instrumentation overhead stays within the strategy's performance mitigation bound (p99 < 5 ms,\n70\t  async emission otherwise).\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- [P0] Observability metrics functional: token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key\n75\t  lifecycle events.\n76\t- [P1] Observability logging functional (maas-api portion: authentication events, API key\n77\t  validation, subscription selection).\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba431fd5c6e583b5","agent_id":"a56ac38aeba4300c7","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e