{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90dd641ad849a12c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n3\ttitle: Deploy and validate MaaS on CKS and AKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E004\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E005\n14\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: rewrite\n17\t  fallback_approach: 'If RHCL official xKS support is not committed, deploy Kuadrant\n18\t    via the fallback ladder: standalone Authorino + Limitador via Helm, or direct\n19\t    Envoy ext_authz integration as contingency; the escalation to product leadership\n20\t    is recorded and the deployment approach rewritten accordingly. The second Investigation\n21\t    dependency also bears on this epic: if the MaaS 3.4 baseline changeability assessment\n22\t    finds the Tenant CRD frozen, the tier-mapping validation falls back to the documented\n23\t    group claim format instead of a configured groupClaimPath, and if the stable\n24\t    build is delayed the validation target falls back to the RC build per the strategy''s\n25\t    timing risk.'\n26\tai_signals:\n27\t  change_specificity: 1\n28\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n29\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n30\t  existing_foundation: 1\n31\t  open_questions: 0\n32\t  external_dependency: -1\n33\t  human_process_gates: 0\n34\t  repo_access: 1\n35\t  architecture_claims: 1\n36\timplementation_type: null\n37\tinvestigation_signals: null\n38\tai_implementability: High\n39\tai_implementability_score: 4\n40\tjira_key: null\n41\tbranch: null\n42\t---\n43\t# Deploy and validate MaaS on CKS and AKS\n44\t\n45\t## Description\n46\t\n47\tDeploys MaaS via the Helm charts on CKS first (the priority platform, with Istio GatewayClass and\n48\tmTLS configuration for CoreWeave's service mesh), then on AKS, and validates core MaaS\n49\tfunctionality: subscription/tier management, token rate limiting, API key authentication, and\n50\texternal OIDC authentication. The Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) underlay is\n51\tdeployed using the mechanism confirmed by the RHCL xKS support validation, with the strategy's\n52\tfallback ladder (standalone Authorino + Limitador via Helm; direct Envoy ext_authz contingency)\n53\tavailable if official RHCL support is not committed. Failure-mode validation and the\n54\tengineering-delta documentation (what works, what breaks, and the code/configuration changes\n55\tneeded) are carried as a separate follow-up epic that consumes this epic's deployed instances.\n56\t\n57\t## Scope\n58\t\n59\t- Deploy MaaS on CKS via Helm with OIDC configuration and the Istio GatewayClass (including TLS\n60\t  and mTLS configuration for Istio control-plane integration).\n61\t- Deploy MaaS on AKS via Helm (GatewayClass per platform: `azure-application-gateway` or\n62\t  `envoy-gateway`).\n63\t- Validate core functionality on both platforms: subscription management, token rate limiting,\n64\t  API key lifecycle, OIDC authentication, tier mapping with OIDC group claims.\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- Given a CKS cluster with RHCL/Kuadrant and Gateway API (Istio) installed, when MaaS is deployed\n69\t  via Helm chart with OIDC configuration, then the maas-api and maas-controller pods are running\n70\t  and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n71\t- Given an AKS cluster with RHCL/Kuadrant and Gateway API installed, when MaaS is deployed via\n72\t  Helm chart with OIDC configuration, then the maas-api and maas-controller pods are running and\n73\t  healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n74\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with OIDC configured, when a user authenticates with a\n75\t  valid OIDC JWT token and creates an API key, then the API key is persisted in PostgreSQL and\n76\t  can be used for model inference, measured by a successful inference request using the generated\n77\t  API key.\n78\t- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit,\n79\t  then Limitador returns HTTP 429, measured by monitoring response status codes.\n80\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with OIDC configured and the group-claim mapping approach\n81\t  selected by the baseline changeability assessment in place, when a user whose OIDC token carries\n82\t  group membership authenticates and is assigned a subscription, then tier/subscription management\n83\t  maps the user to the correct tier via OIDC group claims, measured by successful tier/subscription\n84\t  CRUD and tier-based rate limiting enforcement.\n85\t- What works and what breaks during deployment on both platforms is recorded and handed to the\n86\t  failure-mode validation and engineering-delta documentation effort.\n87\t\n88\t## HLR Traceability\n89\t\n90\t- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on CKS.\n91\t- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on AKS.\n92\t- [P0] Token rate limiting functional on xKS.\n93\t- [P0] External OIDC authentication validated for user identity.\n94\t- [P0] API key authentication (`sk-oai-*` flow) functional on xKS.\n95\t- [P1] Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims (validation portion).\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba431fd5c6e583b5","agent_id":"a56ac38aeba4300c7","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"f90b1dd2-87d2-4324-a18d-ce312cb04202","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:20:02.230Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-90dd641ad849a12c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
