{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-877d84f904468641","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E010\n3\ttitle: Structured logging for Authorino and Limitador on xKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: RHCL / OpenShift\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E003\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: 'If the deployed Kuadrant mechanism is the standalone or direct\n17\t    Envoy fallback rather than official RHCL, rewrite the logging configuration for\n18\t    that deployment form; if the components cannot emit the required structured fields,\n19\t    escalate to the RHCL team for an upstream change. The second Investigation dependency\n20\t    also bears on this epic: if CKS Grafana Loki is not accessible for MaaS workload\n21\t    logs, rewrite the log aggregation destination per that investigation''s fallback\n22\t    (dedicated Loki provisioning for the MaaS Dev Preview deployment).'\n23\tai_signals:\n24\t  change_specificity: 1\n25\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n26\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n27\t  existing_foundation: 1\n28\t  open_questions: 0\n29\t  external_dependency: -1\n30\t  human_process_gates: -1\n31\t  repo_access: 1\n32\t  architecture_claims: 0\n33\timplementation_type: null\n34\tinvestigation_signals: null\n35\tai_implementability: Medium\n36\tai_implementability_score: 1\n37\tjira_key: null\n38\tbranch: null\n39\t---\n40\t# Structured logging for Authorino and Limitador on xKS\n41\t\n42\t## Description\n43\t\n44\tConfigures structured logging for the Kuadrant components MaaS depends on — Authorino\n45\tauthentication decisions and Limitador rate limit enforcement — on xKS, formatted for aggregation\n46\tin CKS Grafana Loki. Owned by the RHCL / OpenShift team, which validates the passive Kuadrant\n47\tcomponents (no product code changes expected for Limitador; Authorino changes are configuration)\n48\ton the deployment mechanism confirmed by the RHCL xKS support validation. The logging validation\n49\truns against the deployed MaaS instance and its Kuadrant underlay on CKS — the artifact of the\n50\tCKS/AKS deployment validation — so the configured logging is exercised on the real deployment\n51\ttopology.\n52\t\n53\t## Scope\n54\t\n55\t- Structured logging configuration for Authorino authentication decisions (success/failure,\n56\t  identity, method, reason).\n57\t- Structured logging configuration for Limitador rate limit enforcement (429 responses with\n58\t  exceeded quota).\n59\t- Log format compatible with CKS Grafana Loki aggregation and label-based querying.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with structured logging enabled, when an authentication\n64\t  event occurs (success or failure), then the Authorino log entry includes timestamp, user\n65\t  identity, authentication method, decision (allow/deny), and reason (if denied), measured by\n66\t  querying CKS Grafana Loki with label filters.\n67\t- Rate limit enforcement events (HTTP 429 with exceeded quota) are logged by Limitador in\n68\t  structured form and aggregated in Loki.\n69\t- TokenRateLimitPolicy behavior is confirmed unchanged on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (Limitador\n70\t  requires no code changes).\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- [P1] Observability logging functional (Authorino/Limitador portion: authentication events,\n75\t  rate limit enforcement).\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba431fd5c6e583b5","agent_id":"a56ac38aeba4300c7","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"7b110797-48d3-469f-aaa5-3952af1841c0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:20:06.840Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-877d84f904468641","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"