{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a16e06349df2d25","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E013\n3\ttitle: Failure-mode validation and engineering-delta documentation for MaaS on xKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: -1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 0\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 3\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Failure-mode validation and engineering-delta documentation for MaaS on xKS\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tValidates the strategy's failure-mode acceptance criteria against the deployed MaaS instances on\n35\tCKS and AKS, and documents what works, what breaks, and the engineering delta (code changes,\n36\tconfiguration changes, Helm chart packaging gaps) for MaaS on xKS versus RHOAI MaaS GA. Runs\n37\tagainst the running instances produced by the deployment validation, so failure-mode behavior is\n38\tmeasured on the same topology users will encounter. The engineering-delta findings feed the\n39\tknown-limitations documentation.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Validate failure modes on the deployed instances: OIDC provider unavailability, Limitador pod\n44\t  termination, cert-manager certificate rotation, PostgreSQL unavailability.\n45\t- Document what works vs. what breaks on each platform and the engineering delta (code changes,\n46\t  configuration changes, Helm chart packaging gaps).\n47\t- Hand the findings to the known-limitations documentation effort.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Failure mode — OIDC provider unavailable: API key requests continue to succeed; OIDC requests\n52\t  fail with HTTP 503 and a descriptive error, measured by response status and error body.\n53\t- Failure mode — Limitador pod terminated: inference requests denied with HTTP 503, measured by\n54\t  response status and Envoy logs showing upstream connection failure.\n55\t- Failure mode — cert-manager TLS rotation: active inference requests continue without\n56\t  interruption; new requests succeed with the new certificate, measured by zero connection errors\n57\t  during the rotation window and successful TLS handshake validation post-rotation.\n58\t- Failure mode — PostgreSQL unavailable: API key creation fails with HTTP 503 and existing API\n59\t  key validation fails on cache miss, while OIDC token-based authentication continues to succeed,\n60\t  measured by response status and error logs.\n61\t- What works, what breaks, and the engineering delta are documented for both platforms.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (failure-mode validation portion).\n66\t- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on AKS (failure-mode validation portion).\n67\t- Enables [P1] Known limitations documented (engineering-delta findings feed the documentation).\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba431fd5c6e583b5","agent_id":"a56ac38aeba4300c7","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"b4bf8c3d-eb43-4a7d-8ec0-9ceb33321d12","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:20:09.085Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a16e06349df2d25","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
