{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ef4eb2a559b32c8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-A-E006\n3\ttitle: Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping in MaaS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: 'If the Tenant CRD is frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA (outcome A does not\n16\t    hold), drop this code-change epic and adopt the documentation approach: document\n17\t    the required group claim format and push IdP configuration burden to customers.'\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping in MaaS\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tConditional branch (outcome A: the MaaS 3.4 GA baseline is extensible). Implements configurable\n39\tOIDC group claim path mapping so the MaaSSubscription controller can map rate-limiting tiers to\n40\tuser groups sourced from OIDC tokens with provider-varying claim formats (Entra ID `groups`,\n41\tCognito `cognito:groups`, Google Identity Platform custom claims) instead of Kubernetes RBAC\n42\tgroups.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Add a `groupClaimPath` field to the Tenant CRD (default `auth.identity.groups`).\n47\t- Pass the configured claim path through to the MaaSSubscription controller's CEL predicate\n48\t  generation for tier/subscription mapping.\n49\t- Expose the claim path as a Helm chart value for per-deployment configuration.\n50\t- Document the `groupClaimPath` configuration for deployers (chart value, Tenant CRD field, and\n51\t  the default `auth.identity.groups`), so the identity-flow documentation can reference it for\n52\t  the group-claim specifics rather than duplicating it.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Given an OIDC deployment with a non-standard group claim format and `groupClaimPath` configured\n57\t  to match, a user with group membership authenticating is mapped to the appropriate subscription\n58\t  tier, measured by successful tier-based rate limiting enforcement.\n59\t- The default claim path preserves current RHOAI behavior (backwards compatible, additive change).\n60\t- Tier/subscription CRUD against OIDC group claims is functional.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- [P0] Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (supports Entra ID `groups`, Cognito\n65\t  `cognito:groups`, custom claims).\n66\t- [P1] Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba431fd5c6e583b5","agent_id":"a56ac38aeba4300c7","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"9f7034e4-0d4a-4964-8cad-18bd41a1e503","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:20:12.972Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ef4eb2a559b32c8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
