{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a45ea08b49bfba79","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-B-E006\n3\ttitle: Document required OIDC group claim format for xKS identity providers\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tbranch: B\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the Tenant CRD is extensible in MaaS 3.4 GA (outcome B does\n17\t    not hold), drop this documentation epic and implement the configurable groupClaimPath\n18\t    field in the Tenant CRD and subscription controller instead.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 0\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Document required OIDC group claim format for xKS identity providers\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tConditional branch (outcome B: the Tenant CRD is frozen in MaaS 3.4 GA and cannot be extended).\n39\tDelivers the strategy's stated fallback for group claim mapping: document the required OIDC group\n40\tclaim format and push identity-provider configuration burden to customers, so that customer IdPs\n41\temit groups at the claim path the MaaS subscription controller already reads\n42\t(`auth.identity.groups`).\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Author customer-facing documentation of the required group claim format for MaaS tier mapping\n47\t  on xKS.\n48\t- Per-provider configuration guidance: Entra ID (emitting `groups`), Cognito (mapping\n49\t  `cognito:groups`), Google Identity Platform (custom claims), Keycloak (group claims).\n50\t- Validation guidance for customers to verify their IdP emits the expected claim.\n51\t- Content split with the known-limitations / identity-flow documentation effort: this deliverable\n52\t  owns the per-provider claim-format configuration reference (exact claim path and format,\n53\t  per-IdP guidance, validation steps). The identity-flow document covers the end-to-end flow\n54\t  (OIDC issuer configuration, token validation, API key lifecycle) and references this reference\n55\t  for the group-claim specifics rather than duplicating it.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- The documentation states the exact claim path and format MaaS expects for tier mapping.\n60\t- Configuration guidance covers at least Entra ID, Cognito, and one standards-compliant provider\n61\t  (e.g., Keycloak).\n62\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the MaaS subscription controller's actual\n63\t  predicate behavior.\n64\t- The guidance is validated with at least one real identity provider configuration.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- [P0] Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping (fallback delivery: documented claim format\n69\t  with customer IdP configuration).\n70\t- [P1] Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba431fd5c6e583b5","agent_id":"a56ac38aeba4300c7","session_id":"d2b1376c-e550-4ef4-93a1-44e607f6014e","uuid":"0268f3a2-ad2a-4624-940b-26711df50db9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:20:13.693Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a45ea08b49bfba79","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
